The ascension of the Dawkins was as wondrous as it was indescribable. The records contain apocryphal and contradictory accounts, including one which describes a Vision Splendid of Little Clinton rising from Mother Sarah\'92s arms, glowing like a cherub-shaped night-light, rising regally, as graceful as a dirigible, his penile tether dangling below the hot-air balloon of his chubby bottom, which was as squidgy as a soft jelly-baby. Other accounts say he exploded like a burning ring of fire.\
Alert readers may have noticed we referred to documentary records of the Dawkins\'92 Ascension, but how could such accounts exist? To make room for the vastly improved universe the Dawkins wrought, all witnesses should have been destroyed along with the universe that excreted the Airborne Meritocracy of Ulyssia into existence.\
As it turned out, the remaining 3 Sages of the apocalypse got their prophesies mostly right. What they had not calculated upon was the perfectly reasonable beneficence of Baby Dawkins who, finding that science and reason were not incompatible with compassion and yes, let\'92s dare say it, love\'97even for that most miserable universal constructs\'97the Dawkins spared Sarahs\'92 and Tonys\'92 world, and allowed it the dignity of meeting its own destiny, which turned out to be hugely entertaining, if somewhat embarrassing for anyone who voted and bribed for it.\
And so it came to pass, when the Dawkins filed his plans for a new Creation with the town planners at Multiversal Council Chambers, he discovered there was no need for a demolition of the decrepit fixer-upper he had been endowed, because, in their exact words, 
\f2\i Sure! There\'92s always room for one more
\f1\i0 .\
So in the Dawkins\'92 new project, science and reason indeed triumphed, absent of humanity\'92s obsessive need to burn shit, cut shit down and put fences around shit\'97and despite humanity\'92s lust for threatening the existence of any species, race, or class not their own.\
The history books from the earth of this universe tell no tales of atrocities, because such atrocious things simply never happened. There were no Crusades; no \cf3 Wanggongchang Explosion; no \cf2 Spanish Inquisition; no Taiping Rebellion; no COVID-19; no Tenerife airport disaster; no Mongol conquests; no outsourcing; no Japanese war crimes; no CIA, KGB, FSB or Mossad; no European colonisation of \'91new\'92 worlds; no space shuttle disasters; no Dungan revolt; no wars on terror, drugs, or gender reassignment; and no big oil, big tobacco, big pharma, big fast food, or big K-pop. There were never any digital watches either; presumably because the One Before the One\'97that is, the original clump of genetic memes known as the Original Richard Dawkins (original, yet just a smidge shy of the Best Dawkins Ever, may his deeds be praised)\'97believed Douglas Adams was seven feet tall, and was a wonderful, wonderful man. He also wrote him a fan letter for 
\f2\i Dirk Gently\'92s Holistic Detective Agency
\f1\i0 , and was delighted to receive a fan letter in return from the celebrated member of the Adams family.\
Which is not to say, in the Dawkins\'92 new world such things did not occur as would naturally arise from physics and evolution: notably plagues, floods, fires, earthquakes, volcanic eruptions, amusement park accidents, and erectile dysfuntion. However, no inhabitants of the earth of this universe sought to exploit these, nor magnify the suffering of others during such occurrences; but rather, they cooperatively sought just, effective, and systemically balanced remedies, mitigations and solutions for all such hard times.\
The Elvis of the Dawkins\'92 fresh Godless Garden of Eden fares rather better than most. He never suffered from the genetic lottery that brewed his faulty, in-bred DNA; he grew up in dignity and relative comfort, never losing his childhood home; he was well-educated, learned to read music, and understood nutrition; he grew out of his mother fixation; he got along with Frank Sinatra; he never feared being a father; he was never exploited by avaricious management; there were no Catholics to report him to the FBI director (also there was no FBI); the Estonian word for 
\f2\i pelvis
\f1\i0  (
\f2\i vaagnaluu
\f1\i0 ) did not rhyme with his name; souvenir-hungry mobs never stripped him naked and stole his clothes; he never felt the need to recluse to Graceland the sake of safety; he received and took good medical advice; and he was never conscripted to a feeding frenzy known in other universes as a 
\f2\i war
\f1\i0 . This Elvis lived as happy as he wished, devoting his life to the things he loved most: singing and shakin\'92 that thing; and pulling over speeding drivers, lecturing them, and giving them tickets to which he duly affixed his autograph. This Elvis lived well into his nineties until his final Vegas show at the Kadriog 
\f2\i Pension\'e4ride Mugavusmaja Lugupeetud Vanuritele
\f1\i0  where, during a particularly vigorous performance of 
\f2\i Ale House Rock
\f1\i0  (get over it; there were no jails) he threw his hip so far, it cracked. This poor Elvis would\'92ve fallen straight to the stage, except for an improbable conjunction between a microphone stand and a tangle of industrially sturdy gold chains that hung from his neck and adorned his manly chest. He tragically hanged himself, expiring with the gurgling phrase, 
\f2\i Thank you very much,
\f1\i0  in his constricted throat. It was swift; he was dead before his cape settled. And he died doing what he loved. Of course, he received a standing ovation, at least by those residents of the 
\f2\i Pension\'e4ride Mugavusmaja
\f1\i0  who were still ambulant.\
Any Elvis of any universe deserved whatever (consensual) love and adoration came their way. However it\'92s generally affirmed by anyone whose ability to see the big picture (across, say forty-two gazillion universes), this Elvis\'97of the universe which took the Dawkins seven days to create (if you accept a Creator\'92s Standard Day to be something in the order of five billion years long)\'97was the loveliest. And the happiest.\
